{"G1084":{"id":"G1084","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1084","disambiguated_id":"G1084 =","unique_id":"G1084","headword":"γεννητός","transliteration":"gennētos","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"born","definition_en":"γεννητός, -ή -όν \n (γεννάω), [in LXX: Job.11:2, 12 14:1 15:14 25:4 (ילד)* ;] \nbegotten, born: pl., γ. γυναικῶν (cf. יְלוּד אִשָּׁה, Job.14:1), periphrasis for mankind, Mat.11:11, Luk.7:28 (Cremer, 147).\n (AS)","source_line":1211}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"nascidos","count":2}]},"G1092":{"id":"G1092","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1092","disambiguated_id":"G1092 =","unique_id":"G1092","headword":"γεωργός","transliteration":"geōrgos","lexical_morphology":"G:N-M","gloss_en":"farmer","definition_en":"γεωργός, -οῦ, ὁ \n (γῆ, ἔργω = ἔρδω, to do), [in LXX for אִכָּר, etc. ;] \n __1. a husbandman: 2Ti.2:6, Jas.5:7. \n __2. a vine-dresser (cf. ἀμπελουργός, Luk.13:7): Mat.21:33-35, 38, 40, 41, Mrk.12:1, 2 7, 9, Luk.20:9, 10 14, 16, Jhn.15:1.\n† (AS)","source_line":1221}],"occurrence_count":19,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"lavradores","count":16},{"gloss":"lavrador","count":3}]},"G1342":{"id":"G1342","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1342","disambiguated_id":"G1342 =","unique_id":"G1342","headword":"δίκαιος","transliteration":"dikaios","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"just","definition_en":"δίκαιος, -α, -ον\n (δίκη), [in LXX chiefly for צַדִּיק (for rendering of צַדִּיק in sense of correct, see Deiss., BS, 115 f.); sometimes for נָקִי as Pro.1:11, al. ;] \nin early Gk. writers \n__(a) of persons, observant of δίκη, custom, rule, right, righteous in performing duties to gods and men ; \n __(b) of things, righteous, in accordance with right. \n In NT \n__1. righteous, chiefly in the broad sense, as above, of the person or thing corresponding to the Divine standard of right \n__(a) of persons: of God, Rom.3:26, 1Jn.2:29 Jn 3:7; of Christ, Act.3:14 7:52 22:14, 1Pe.3:18, 1Jn.2:1; of men, Mat.1:19 (Abbott, Essays, 75 f.) Mat.10:41 13:17, 43 13:49, Luk.1:6, 17, Rom.5:7, 1Ti.1:9, Jas.5:6, 1Pe.3:12, 1Jn.3:7, Rev.22:11, al.; δ. καὶ εὐλαβής, Luk.2:25; ἅγιος, Mrk.6:20; ἀγαθός, Luk.23:50; φοβούμενος τ. θεόν, Act.10:22; opposite to ἀμαρτωλοὶ καὶ ἀσεβεῖς, 1Pe.4:18; ἄδικοι, Mat.5:45, Act.24:15; δ. ἐκ πίστεως, Rom.1:17, Gal.3:11, Heb.10:38\" (LXX) ; δ. παρὰ τ. θεῷ, Rom.2:13 \n __(b) of things: ἔργα δ., opposite to πονηρὰ, 1Jn.3:12; ἐντολή, Rom.7:12; metaphorically, αἷμα, Mat.23:35; τὸ δ., Luk.12:57; δ. ἐστιν, Act.4:19, Eph.6:1, Php.1:7; ὅ, Mat.20:4; ὅσα, Php.4:8 \n __2. In narrower sense \n__(a) of persons, as in later cl. writers, just, rendering to each his due: Tit.1:8, 1Jn.1:9; δ. κριτής, 2Ti.4:8 \n __(b) of things: τὸ δ., Col.4:1; δ., sc. ἐστιν, 2Th.1:6; κρίσις δ., Jhn.5:30; ὁδοί, Rev.15:3 \n SYN.: ἀγαθός (which see), καλός, χρηστός (Cremer, 183, 690). (AS)","source_line":1474}],"occurrence_count":79,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"justo","count":51},{"gloss":"justos","count":25},{"gloss":"justa","count":2},{"gloss":"justas","count":1}]},"G1451":{"id":"G1451","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1451","disambiguated_id":"G1451 =","unique_id":"G1451","headword":"ἐγγύς","transliteration":"engus","lexical_morphology":"G:PREP / G:A","gloss_en":"near","definition_en":"ἐγγύς, adv., \n [in LXX chiefly for קָרוֹב ;] \nnear; \n__1. of place: Jhn.19:20, 42; as prep. with genitive (M, Pr., 99), Luk.19:11, Jhn.3:23 6:19, 23 11:18, 54, Act.1:12; with dative, Act.9:38 27:8; superl., ἔγγιστα, Mrk.6:36, WH, mg.; metaphorically, ֹοἱ ἐ., opposite to οἱ μακράν, Eph.2:17; ἐ. γίνεσθαι, Eph.2:13; ἐ. σου τὸ ῥῆμα, Rom.10:8 (LXX). \n __2. Of time: Mat.24:32 26:18, Mrk.13:28, 29 Luk.21:30, 31 Jhn.2:13 6:4 7:2 11:55, Rev.1:3 22:10; ὁ κύριος ἐ., Php.4:5; before ἐπὶ θύραις, Mat.24:33; compar., ἐγγύτερον (neut. of adj. -ος, used adverbially), Rom.13:11 (cf. R, txt.); as prep. with genitive, ἐ. κατάρας, Heb.6:8; ἀφανισμοῦ, Heb.8:13 (cf. Cremer, 223).\n† (AS)","source_line":1583}],"occurrence_count":30,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"perto","count":21},{"gloss":"já-perto","count":3},{"gloss":"junto","count":2},{"gloss":"já","count":1},{"gloss":"aproximando","count":1},{"gloss":"era","count":1},{"gloss":"próximo","count":1}]},"G1712":{"id":"G1712","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1712","disambiguated_id":"G1712 =","unique_id":"G1712","headword":"ἐμπόριον","transliteration":"emporion","lexical_morphology":"G:N-N","gloss_en":"marketplace/trade","definition_en":"ἐμπόριον, -ον, τό\n (ἔμπορος) [in LXX: Deu.33:19 (סָפַן), Eze.27:3 (רָכַל); ἐ. εἶναι, Isa.23:17 (זָנָה)* ;] \na trading place, exchange: οἶκος ἐμπορίου, Jhn.2:16.†\n (AS)","source_line":1853}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"comércio","count":1}]},"G1833":{"id":"G1833","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1833","disambiguated_id":"G1833 =","unique_id":"G1833","headword":"ἐξετάζω","transliteration":"exetazō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to find out","definition_en":"ἐξ-ετάζω\n (ἐτάζω (rare), to examine), [in LXX: Deu.13:14-15 Deu.19:18, 1Ch.28:9 A (דָּרַשׁ), דָּרַשׁ), Psa.11:5-6 (בָּחַן), Wis.6:3, Sir.3:21, al. ;] \nto examine closely, inquire carefully (of ): before περί (with ἀκριβῶς), Mat.2:8; before τίς, Mat.10:11; with accusative of person(s), Jhn.21:12.†\n SYN.: ἀνακρίνω, ἐραυνάω (see DCG, ii, 594b) (AS)","source_line":1974}],"occurrence_count":3,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"investigai","count":1},{"gloss":"informai","count":1},{"gloss":"perguntar","count":1}]},"G2042":{"id":"G2042","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2042","disambiguated_id":"G2042 =","unique_id":"G2042","headword":"ἐρεθίζω","transliteration":"erethizō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to provoke/irritate","definition_en":"ἐρεθίζω \n [in LXX: Dan LXX 11:10, 25 (גָּרָה hithp.), 1Ma.15:40, 2Ma.14:17, etc. ;] \n__1. to stir up, provoke (as in cl.): Col.3:21. \n __2. In good sense (cf. ἐρεθισμός, excitement, in MGr.), to stir up, stimulate: 2Co.9:2.†\n (AS)","source_line":2183}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"começou","count":1},{"gloss":"provoqueis","count":1}]},"G2173":{"id":"G2173","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2173","disambiguated_id":"G2173 =","unique_id":"G2173","headword":"εὔχρηστος","transliteration":"euchrēstos","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"helpful","definition_en":"εὔ-χρηστος, -ον\n (εὖ, χράομαι), [in LXX: Pro.31:13 (חֵפֶץ), Wis.13:13 * ;] \nuseful, serviceable: with dative of person(s), 2Ti.2:21; id. before εἰς, with dative of thing(s), 2Ti.4:11; opposite to ἄχρηστος, Phm 11.†\n (AS)","source_line":2315}],"occurrence_count":3,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"útil","count":2},{"gloss":"uso","count":1}]},"G2466":{"id":"G2466","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2466","disambiguated_id":"G2466 = the Greek of","unique_id":"H3485G","headword":"Ἰσαχάρ","transliteration":"Isachar","lexical_morphology":"N:N-M-P","gloss_en":"Issachar","definition_en":"Ἰσσαχάρ (Rec. Ἰσαχ-, Ἰσασχ- (Elz.), T, -άχαρ), ὁ indecl. (FlJ, Ἰσάχαρις, Ἰσάσχ-) (Heb. יִשָּׂשכָר, Gen.30:18), \n Issachar: Rev.7:7.†\n (AS)","source_line":2632}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"Issacar","count":1}]},"G2905":{"id":"G2905","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2905","disambiguated_id":"G2905 =","unique_id":"G2905","headword":"κραυγάζω","transliteration":"kraugazō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to shout","definition_en":"κραυγάζω (κραυγή) \n [in LXX: Est.3:13 (רוּעַ hi.)* ;] = κράζω \n__1. of animals, to bay, to croak, etc. \n __2. Of men, to cry out, shout: Mat.12:19, Jhn.12:13 19:15 Act.22:23; before λέγων, Jhn.18:40 19:6, 12; καὶ λέγων, Luk.4:41 (WH, κράζ -); φωνῇ μεγάλῃ, Jhn.11:43 (cf. Abbott, JV, 269 f.).†\n (AS)","source_line":3100}],"occurrence_count":9,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"clamaram","count":2},{"gloss":"gritavam","count":2},{"gloss":"gritará","count":1},{"gloss":"saíam