77","disambiguated_id":"G4977 =","unique_id":"G4977","headword":"σχίζω","transliteration":"schizō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to split","definition_en":"σχίζω \n [in LXX chiefly for בָּקַע ;] \nto cleave, rend: Mat.27:51, Mrk.1:10 15:38, Luk.5:36 23:45, Jhn.19:24 21:11; metaphorically, in pass., to be divided into factions, Act.14:4 23:7.† \n (AS)","source_line":5129}],"occurrence_count":11,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"rasgou","count":5},{"gloss":"fenderam","count":1},{"gloss":"abrirem","count":1},{"gloss":"pô","count":1},{"gloss":"partamos","count":1},{"gloss":"rompeu","count":1},{"gloss":"dividiu","count":1}]},"G5052":{"id":"G5052","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G5052","disambiguated_id":"G5052 =","unique_id":"G5052","headword":"τελεσφορέω","transliteration":"telesphoreō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to mature","definition_en":"τελεσφορέω, -ῶ\n (τέλος, φέρω) [in LXX: 4Ma.13:20 * ;] \n__(a) of plants, to bring fruit to perfection (Theophr.): Luk.8:14 \n __(b) of females, to bear perfect offspring (Artemid.; 4Mac, l.with).†\n (AS)","source_line":5204}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"produzem","count":1}]},"G5302":{"id":"G5302","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G5302","disambiguated_id":"G5302 =","unique_id":"G5302","headword":"ὑστερέω","transliteration":"hustereō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to lack","definition_en":"ὑστερέω, -ῶ\n (ὕστερος), [in LXX for חָסֵר, חָדַל etc. ;] \nto come late, be behind (opposite to προτερέω, φθάνω; with genitive of thing(s), for; with genitive of person(s), later than). \n Metaphorical, \n __1. of persons, \n __(a) absol., to come short, fail: Heb.4:1; before ἀπό, Heb.12:15.; \n __(b) with genitive of person(s), to come short of, be inferior to: 2Co.11:5; οὐδέν (in nothing, in no respect), 2Co.12:11; \n __(with) with reference to things, to come short (of ), be in want (of ): with accusative of thing(s), Mat.19:20 (Sir.51:24); with genitive of thing(s), Luk.22:35; so mid. (Diod., FlJ), Rom.3:23; absol., to be in want, suffer want, Luk.15:14, 1Co.8:8, 2Co.11:8, Heb.11:37 (Sir.11:11); opposite to περισσεύειν, Php.4:12; before ἐν, 1Co.1:7. \n __2. Of things, \n __(a) to fail, be lacking: Jhn.2:3; with accusative of person(s) (see Swete, in l; Mozley, Psa.42:1-11), Mrk.10:21; \n __(b) to be inferior: mid., 1Co.12:24 (cf. ἀφ-υστερέω).†\n (AS)","source_line":5458}],"occurrence_count":16,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"falta","count":4},{"gloss":"sofrer-necessidade","count":2},{"gloss":"fui-inferior","count":2},{"gloss":"tivestes-falta","count":1},{"gloss":"faltado","count":1},{"gloss":"destituídos","count":1},{"gloss":"nos-falta","count":1},{"gloss":"tendo-necessidade","count":1},{"gloss":"trás","count":1},{"gloss":"necessitados","count":1},{"gloss":"perca","count":1}]},"G5459":{"id":"G5459","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G5459","disambiguated_id":"G5459 =","unique_id":"G5459","headword":"φωσφόρος","transliteration":"phōsphoros","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"light-bearing","definition_en":"φωσ-φόρος, -ον\n (φῶς, φέρω), \nlight-bringing; as subst., ὁ φ., the morning star (Plat., al.; cf. ἐωσφόρος, Isa.14:12, Job.3:9, Psa.110:3): metaphorically, 2Pe.1:19 (see Mayor, in l).†\n (AS)","source_line":5625}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"estrela","count":1}]},"G5578":{"id":"G5578","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G5578","disambiguated_id":"G5578 =","unique_id":"G5578","headword":"ψευδοπροφήτης","transliteration":"pseudoprophētēs","lexical_morphology":"G:N-M","gloss_en":"false prophet","definition_en":"ψευδο-προφήτης, -ου, ὁ \n [in LXX: Zec.13:2, Jer.1:9 (Jer.6:13, al.) (נָבִיא)* ;] \na false prophet (= cl. ψευδόμαντις): Mat.7:15 24:11, 24, Mrk.13:22 (see Swete, in l), Luk.6:26, Act.13:6, 2Pe.2:1, 1Jn.4:1, Rev.16:13 19:20 20:10 †\n (AS)","source_line":5748}],"occurrence_count":11,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"falsos-profetas","count":7},{